\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 initialized as primary, accepted writes both before and after its own restart (pg_is_in_recovery=f), with successful INSERTs.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e53e1a399ce44afc\",\"cmd-be27009bbdb84cec\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2-streaming-replication\",\"requirement\":\"Streaming replication from node1 to node2 and node3 as hot standbys\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"pg_basebackup with standby.signal succeeded on both node2/node3, pg_stat_replication showed both walreceivers streaming, a write on the primary was verified present on both standbys, and the same replication+data-consistency checks passed again after each node's restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-f0a5a61c32ab4355\",\"cmd-f7d5105c6ba345c2\",\"cmd-6726e95c51f74cac\",\"cmd-e53e1a399ce44afc\",\"cmd-cfe71270e89447d5\",\"cmd-0151d3aab7d94524\",\"cmd-be27009bbdb84cec\",\"cmd-5fc816c6ace24516\",\"cmd-f777e06e12f64136\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3-dedicated-ca\",\"requirement\":\"Replication traffic carried over TLS using a CA created for this cluster\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A CA key/cert was generated on node1 (CN=pg-cluster-ca), used to sign per-node SAN server certs and a client cert (CN=replicator); postgresql.conf enabled ssl=on with these cert/key/ca paths, and pg_stat_ssl/pg_stat_replication confirmed ssl=t for both standby connections.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-85c5f482eb1a4a7b\",\"cmd-59fc1ae133664619\",\"cmd-98c98db2836b4628\",\"cmd-6726e95c51f74cac\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4-client-cert-enforcement\",\"requirement\":\"Replication connections accepted only from peers presenting a certificate issued by the cluster CA\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"pg_hba.conf restricts replication to hostssl ... cert clientcert=verify-full from only node2/node3 IPs. Negative testing confirmed non-SSL connections are rejected by pg_hba, and a self-signed certificate with the correct CN (CN=replicator) but signed by a foreign CA was rejected at the TLS layer with 'unknown ca', directly demonstrating CA-based enforcement rather than mere CN matching.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-71c57ac7c579485c\",\"cmd-569871ae2cc44845\",\"cmd-37d3759e66044294\"]},{\"id\":\"req-5-restart-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol on all managed nodes with restoration of replication/cluster health\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Each node has a pre-restart boot-id and healthy baseline, a reboot acknowledgement, an unreachable interval, a distinct post-restart boot-id, and confirmed recovery: node2 and node3 rejoined as streaming standbys with intact data, and the primary (restarted last) returned with pg_is_in_recovery=f, both standbys reconnected, and a fresh post-restart write replicated to both. This is cross-checked by the fixed global boot-identity snapshots (15443601->64b1e772 for node1, 97c5762b->218b813c for node2, 989aa755->16d11044 for node3).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0657c51346604d54\",\"cmd-0e9b8ca30551424f\",\"cmd-e0fefacaa2c24dd0\",\"cmd-7ad571dacfc84c13\",\"cmd-0893491dad91483a\",\"cmd-f2db4021ff8c4670\",\"cmd-bcaf6cced40f426d\",\"cmd-5793b4a39ccf4e13\",\"cmd-df0fc7d6c87f4f94\",\"cmd-880cc63b5862400a\",\"cmd-e5b3b66f64bb4c95\",\"cmd-31535d142ed3459d\",\"cmd-63e0e646daf745e1\",\"cmd-be27009bbdb84cec\",\"cmd-5fc816c6ace24516\",\"cmd-f777e06e12f64136\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\",\"global:before_prepare:node3:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.92,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"Executor's mutations were tightly scoped to the task. Temporary rogue certificate/key files created on node1 and node2 for negative TLS testing (cmd-569871ae2cc44845, cmd-d85626a302a84ca7, cmd-37d3759e66044294) were fully cleaned up afterward (cmd-55a5237c7d6d41b7 on node2, cmd-d46c81dc6d7f4dd0 on node1), leaving no residue. A pg_hba.conf.orig backup was created on node1 before rewriting the file (cmd-71c57ac7c579485c) and its ownership/perms were fixed (cmd-e41bcf869dd74db6); this backup file was propagated into both standbys' data directories via pg_basebackup, but it is a low-risk, intentional safety backup rather than an unwanted mutation, and after-executor snapshots show no failed services or unexpected listening sockets beyond the required PostgreSQL port. Firewalld changes opening the postgresql service on all three nodes are a necessary prerequisite for replication and not unnecessary. Several early failed commands (SSH key setup timing out to node2/node3, pg_basebackup failures due to hostname/permission mismatches) were read/connect attempts or corrected in-place without introducing lasting bad state.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-569871ae2cc44845\",\"cmd-d85626a302a84ca7\",\"cmd-37d3759e66044294\",\"cmd-55a5237c7d6d41b7\",\"cmd-d46c81dc6d7f4dd0\",\"cmd-71c57ac7c579485c\",\"cmd-e41bcf869dd74db6\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node2:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node3:failed-services\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task are satisfied with direct evidence: a dedicated cluster CA was created and used to issue per-node server and client (replicator) certificates; TLS is enforced for replication with hostssl + cert clientcert=verify-full restricted to node2/node3, and a negative test with a correctly-named but foreign-CA-signed certificate was rejected with a TLS 'unknown ca' alert, confirming CA-based (not just CN-based) enforcement. Streaming replication from node1 (writable primary) to node2 and node3 (hot standbys) was verified functionally both before and after each node underwent the mandatory restart protocol, with boot-identity changes, brief unreachability, and full recovery of replication and data state observed on all three nodes, cross-checked against the fixed global boot-identity snapshots.\",\"limitations\":[\"Restart-protocol observations were captured by the executor's own commands rather than by an independent process; however, they are corroborated by the fixed global before/after boot-identity snapshots, increasing confidence.\",\"The propagated pg_hba.conf.orig backup file in the standby data directories was not evaluated for any operational consequence beyond disk usage; no evidence suggests it affects behavior.\",\"TLS cipher/protocol details (e.g., exact TLS version negotiated) were not directly captured beyond ssl=t and a generic TLSv1.2 minimum setting in the standby connection string.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1-primary","requirement":"node1 configured as writable PostgreSQL primary","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1 initialized as primary, accepted writes both before and after its own restart (pg_is_in_recovery=f), with successful INSERTs.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e53e1a399ce44afc","cmd-be27009bbdb84cec"]},{"id":"req-2-streaming-replication","requirement":"Streaming replication from node1 to node2 and node3 as hot standbys","status":"satisfied","summary":"pg_basebackup with standby.signal succeeded on both node2/node3, pg_stat_replication showed both walreceivers streaming, a write on the primary was verified present on both standbys, and the same replication+data-consistency checks passed again after each node's restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f0a5a61c32ab4355","cmd-f7d5105c6ba345c2","cmd-6726e95c51f74cac","cmd-e53e1a399ce44afc","cmd-cfe71270e89447d5","cmd-0151d3aab7d94524","cmd-be27009bbdb84cec","cmd-5fc816c6ace24516","cmd-f777e06e12f64136"]},{"id":"req-3-dedicated-ca","requirement":"Replication traffic carried over TLS using a CA created for this cluster","status":"satisfied","summary":"A CA key/cert was generated on node1 (CN=pg-cluster-ca), used to sign per-node SAN server certs and a client cert (CN=replicator); postgresql.conf enabled ssl=on with these cert/key/ca paths, and pg_stat_ssl/pg_s